===persian===

وقتی بلور ماه
در چشمه ها شکست....
وقتی شب سیاه....
در غارها و سایه گهارها نشست....
وقتی که مرغ شب...
ابریشم نوای دل آویز خویش را ....
بر پیله طلایی صدها ستاره بست
من از نشیب دره بسوی تو میدوم
با اسب راهوار...
لرزان و بی قرار
دیوانه وار می پرم از سنگچین رود.
تا در کنار چشمه نمانی به انتظار

تویسرکان تابستان ۱۳۴۱

برای مریم

===machine===

When the moon crystal
broke in the springs....
When the black night....
Sat in the caves and shadows of the caves....
When the night bird...
The silk of its heart-rending song....
It tied hundreds of stars to the golden cocoon
I run towards you from the valley slope
On a walking horse...
Shaking and restless
I jump like a madman from the river's cobblestones.
So that you don't stay by the spring, waiting

Twiserkan, summer 1341
For Maryam

===lantern===

When the crystal of the moon
shattered in the springs...
when the black night
settled into the caves and their shadowed hollows...
when the bird of night
bound the silk of its beguiling song
to the golden cocoon of a hundred stars —
I come running to you down the valley's slope
on a swift-paced horse,
trembling, unable to rest,
leaping like a madman over the river's stepping-stones,
so you won't be left waiting by the spring.

Tuyserkan, summer 1341
For Maryam

